  "headline_finding": "Both independent reviewers confirmed and sharpened this Coordinator's own pre-review finding: EXP-MONO-670aa6's declared primary test (Stage-2 null-object gate, Stage-3 Holm/Bonferroni real-arm test) had ZERO statistical power by construction (permutation p-value floor unconditionally exceeds every declared family's Holm threshold), and its panel-independence claim failed totally (100% prime/B/t_used collision across matched curve pairs, plus 58% supersingular contamination of the j0 arm, newly found by the Validator). Stage 0 and the dual-path check on the 100 real-arm cells held. K3/K4 remains open after two consecutive experiments failing for two distinct, documented reasons; accumulated evidence leans mildly, non-conclusively, toward no exceptional locus. A design-time floor-vs-threshold check (KN-TECH-95a42b) is named to prevent recurrence, and the identical defect was found, unremarked, in an already-closed prior record (documented via an addendum to KN-TECH-7745e6, not a reopening).",
